                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.001/54: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Reber</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-03T17:00:00-05:00">December 3, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>109. Your telegrams 168 and 169. Until the receipt of further instructions do not
                    address new officials by title. The Department does not wish to restrict your
                    informal dealings but desires to consider the constitutionality of the change of
                    Government. Please inform the Department with reference thereto.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
